    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The task is composition of f(x)=x^2-3 with four different g, plus a domain statement for each. Part a is direct substitution. Parts b and d involve a square root that cancels with the squaring, so the student must see that the simplified expression still carries the domain restriction of the inner function. Part c needs the exclusion x≠2 from the reciprocal. The hardest essential demand is the 'simplified form hides the inner-domain restriction' step, which is the same as in p26-q5, whose part is repeated here. It is a step above the plain composition-and-domain parts of p26-q4, where the domain comes directly from the simplified expression. It is below p20-q25, which also asks the student to decide which composite does not exist.",
